# FreeCAD: always reload show model at end of answer

**Mandatory last step of the turn** — do not wait for the user to ask.

Whenever this turn changes or discusses the FreeCAD model the user is viewing (`show_jgb37_gui.py`, `.FCStd`, geometry under `3d_model/freecad/`), **before finishing the user-facing answer**:

1. Finish code/model edits first.
2. **Save** the current FreeCAD document so user Placement / visibility are on disk (see below).
3. **Kill** all FreeCAD processes: `freecad`, `FreeCAD`, `freecadcmd`.
4. **Start-Process** FreeCAD with the show script (rebuilds + restores Placement via `apply_preserved_state`).

Do this at the **end of every such answer** so the user never stares at a stale window.

## Save before kill (required)

User may have moved/hidden parts. Before `Stop-Process`, send **Ctrl+S** to the FreeCAD window:

```powershell
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms
$p = Get-Process -Name freecad,FreeCAD -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object -First 1
if ($p -and $p.MainWindowHandle -ne 0) {
  Add-Type @"
using System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices;
public class FcWin {
  [DllImport("user32.dll")] public static extern bool SetForegroundWindow(IntPtr hWnd);
}
"@
  [FcWin]::SetForegroundWindow($p.MainWindowHandle) | Out-Null
  Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 300
  [System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait("^s")
  Start-Sleep -Seconds 1
}
```

## Paths

- Script: `d:\Project\coutingmachine\3d_model\freecad\show_jgb37_gui.py`
- Doc: `d:\Project\coutingmachine\3d_model\freecad\out\jgb37_motor_bracket.FCStd`
- Exe: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\FreeCAD 1.1\bin\freecad.exe`

```powershell
Get-Process -Name freecad,FreeCAD,freecadcmd -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force
Start-Process -FilePath "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\FreeCAD 1.1\bin\freecad.exe" `
  -ArgumentList "`"d:\Project\coutingmachine\3d_model\freecad\show_jgb37_gui.py`""
```

## When it does NOT apply

- Pure docs / git / non-CAD work with no FreeCAD model involvement
- User explicitly says not to reopen FreeCAD
